The scatter plot shows training hours per week and race time for a group of runners. Describe the form, strength and direction of the association.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=6mm,y=6mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(8,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,6);
\node[below] at (4,-0.4) {Training hours per week};
\node[rotate=90] at (-0.6,3) {Race time (min)};
\foreach \p in {(0.8,5.2),(1.4,4.9),(2,4.3),(2.6,4.1),(3.2,3.5),(3.8,3.2),(4.4,2.9),(5,2.3),(5.6,2.1),(6.2,1.5),(6.8,1.3)} {\fill[black] \p circle (1.8pt);}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

